<title>INDIA: India Reliance jumps 4 pct on bonus news.</title>
<headline>India Reliance jumps 4 pct on bonus news.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Reliance Industries Ltd soared 15.5 rupees, or 4.3 percent, to 382 after the petrochemicals giant announced a bonus equity issue in the proportion of one share for every share held.  </p>
<p>&quot;The news is slightly better than expected. I think the stock still has some steam left in it,&quot; Vetri Subramaniam, vice-president equity sales at SSKI Securities Pvt Ltd.</p>
<p>&quot;My dear shareholders I'm delighted to report to you ...my board has recommended a bonus issue in the ratio of one-for-one,&quot; chairman Dhirubhai Ambani told shareholders.</p>
<p>At 0915 GMT the Reliance was up 16 rupees at 382.50.</p>
<p>--Bombay newsroom +91-22-265-9000</p>
